        "runId": "ada-en-mw96khaf-1a0l7x",
        "model": "gpt-6"
      },
      "text": "Depart San José early in the morning, at around 06:00.\n\nTravel by air-conditioned bus with a bilingual naturalist guide.\n\nThe route passes through Braulio Carrillo National Park, with views of mountain slopes and dense vegetation.\n\nStop for breakfast at Selva Tropical restaurant, where you may see butterflies and tropical flowers.\n\nAfter breakfast, continue through banana-growing areas to the Caño Blanco pier.\n\nAt Caño Blanco, board a covered boat and follow the Tortuguero canals to your lodge.\n\nExpect to arrive between 12:30 and 13:00.\n\nAfter lunch, visit the Caribbean Conservation Corporation's turtle museum and the village of Tortuguero.\n\nReturn to the lodge at around 17:30.\n\nSpend some time by the pool or at the bar. Dinner is served from 19:30 to 21:00.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast, lunch and dinner."
    },
